  "notes": [
    "The direct contract's constructor fixed its TLN token, LP token, both reserve-reading pairs, SmartNode and qualification contract. Its 10,785-byte runtime is absent before deployment and has the same hash at deployment and immediately before the exploit; later governance calls changed eligibility thresholds, not the causal reserve-pricing logic or its fixed inputs.",
    "TlnSwap is a direct non-proxy contract whose constructor fixed the TLN, VOW and VUSD tokens and the USDT/VOW pair used by _vowToLock(). Its 13,971-byte runtime is absent in the preceding block and hashes identically at deployment and immediately before the exploit; it exposes no setter for those inputs or the collateral calculation.",
    "TlnSwap's VUSD balance fell exactly 3,251,534.902745099463206875, but VUSD had no reliable external dollar market, so it is not valued at its nominal peg. The recorded loss is instead the attacker's exact net realised proceeds. On BSC, the two sweep transactions moved 107,881.749956792323205771 USDT and 1,463,280.244257269082062875 VOW from the attack contract to the EOA. The EOA sold all USDT and 3,280.244257269082062875 VOW for 184.838953341954182596 BNB, then bridged exactly 1,460,000 VOW to Ethereum and sold it in 61 transactions for 171.439728226688515854 ETH. The 2 BNB transferred into the attack contract during setup bought the LP position later surrendered to staking and is attacker-supplied capital, so it is removed from the BNB component. Gas and bridge fees are disposal costs and are not subtracted. Incident-time DefiLlama prices value the resulting 182.838953341954182596 BNB and 171.439728226688515854 ETH at $748,229.12. Early reports of approximately $200,000 to $280,000 did not follow the VOW bridge and liquidation.",
    "The staking runtime is unverified on BscScan; its fixed inputs and reward calculation were reviewed from constructor bytecode, runtime decompilation, archive calls and the exploit trace.",
    "Not the knot: one link of the conjunctive failure; the sibling with the latest age reset supplies the incident's single observation."
